Vote: REQUEST_CHANGES

- `docs/design/printer-controls-section.md:355-360,543-545` only defines idle/pending/printing/offline. It never specifies the capability-gated states Hudson needs for #284-#286 (`supportsTemperatureControl == false` or `supportsMovement == false`), so the implementer still has to guess whether those subgroups hide or render disabled.
- `docs/design/printer-controls-section.md:339-344,540-541` sets Jog's default step to `10` / `10.0`, but #286 locks the default at `1 mm`. That is a build-breaking mismatch for the first implementation.
- `docs/design/printer-controls-section.md:231-235` says Home XY and Home Z call `POST /api/printers/{id}/home`. The backend/service contract for #281 uses dedicated `/homexy` and `/homez` routes, so this spec currently points Hudson at the wrong API.

